+## Complete read-only compositor IPC probe (V11)
+
+A credential/inode proof on the compositor IPC socket does not authorize closing
+a zero-request connection: the actual server may write an error after disconnect.
+The IPC guard must send exactly nonempty `j/version`, consume a bounded complete
+JSON reply through server EOF, then validate exact compositor PID/start and socket
+inode again before closing. Empty/malformed/oversized replies, errors, missing EOF
+or peer/session change refuse the native runtime before actor effects. The maximum
+reply is 65536 bytes and the whole exchange has a 0.5 second deadline. This is a
+read-only version observation; no compositor dispatcher/window/input command.
+The separate Wayland socket credential probe sends no protocol messages and is
+closed without creating registry/output/surface resources.
